WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.720
# Script

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:01.140
## Overview

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:01.590
---

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:07.080
The One Piece Live Action! I’ve JUST&nbsp;
finished binging all 8 episodes of it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.860
starting SECONDS after it came out and even&nbsp;
though I swore to myself that I would get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.760
some sleep first and then share my thoughts&nbsp;
about it with all of you in the mornin—-yeah&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:21.180
i should have known that was not going to&nbsp;
happen. We need to talk about this show and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:27.420
if it ended up being another let down proving&nbsp;
that live action just doesnt work for anime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:34.140
or if it somehow actually managed to live&nbsp;
up to its hype and break the curse once and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:39.240
for all. But of course if you haven't seen all 8&nbsp;
episodes yet, you hereby have been spoiler warned.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:45.000
And we begin with the very first episode, arguably&nbsp;
the single most important one, because if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.700
don’t like the pilot, you probably won’t keep&nbsp;
watching, right? So how did it do? I think right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:58.860
off the bat with the first opening sequence I let&nbsp;
out a big sigh of relieve. Even though there was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:05.220
lot still to come, I knew that at least visually&nbsp;
and music wise, this was not going to suck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:12.360
which with all things that might go wrong, was&nbsp;
an important win. Fantastic animation right into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:17.880
that beautiful long drone shot straight into Logue&nbsp;
Town where of course we kick things off with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:24.960
execution of Gol D. Roger, just like in the manga&nbsp;
and anime. And Garp blasting in a thick Scottish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:30.660
accent was NOT was I expected to hear right out&nbsp;
of the gate at all. And i did not expect how big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:36.480
of a role this character would be playing in this&nbsp;
series. Now we of course already saw a lot of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.140
sequence in the trailer, but there are still a&nbsp;
few things that stood out to me right off the bat:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:46.080
First of all, thank god they fixed the color&nbsp;
grading of the entire show. In the trailers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:52.620
everything looked very fake and clean, but&nbsp;
clearly they were still polishing things behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:58.740
the scenes, because the entire show had a really&nbsp;
nice desaturated look with a lot of character and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:04.440
they clearly also added in more smoke, fog and&nbsp;
other visual elements to connect everything in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:10.320
frame together. This was one of my biggest&nbsp;
fears going into this show, and they luckily&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:17.040
ended up nailing it. Also, in this scene, but&nbsp;
also throughout the series, the music was just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:23.340
on point. A lot of tracks inspired by and mixed&nbsp;
with the official one piece score, for example we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:28.140
here binks sake during luffy’s flashback with&nbsp;
shanks, but also a bunch of original music,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:35.220
that was nicely inspired by the characters they&nbsp;
included: A jazzy french-like tune in the baratie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:41.400
or the spanish theme in the scene with Mihawk as a&nbsp;
nod to him being based on a Spanish conquistador.&nbsp;

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:48.120
But anyways, what also became very clear within&nbsp;
the first 3 minutes of watching: The One Piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:54.240
Live Action is BRUTAL. Like what the.. Just&nbsp;
in this first episode alone, we get Roger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:03:00.960
being executed pretty gruesomely, Alvida crushing&nbsp;
someones head with her club and Zoro just straight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:08.460
out cutting the Baroque Works agent Mr 7 in half.&nbsp;
Which overall leads to this really strange mix of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:15.480
gory seriousness, and the lighthearted comedy and&nbsp;
look of many one piece characters that we know.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:22.200
Which feels bizarre, but honestly is just exactly&nbsp;
what i had been hoping for: Keeping the series’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:27.840
fun side, while still appealing to an adult&nbsp;
audience and making things a bit more mature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:34.500
though I didn’t quite expect things to go as&nbsp;
mature as full on nude Helmeppo, playing with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.560
his sword. [ play pornhub intro before scene with&nbsp;
Zoro walking in on helmeppo] But going back to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:43.920
fights, the battles and choreographies were also&nbsp;
insanely well done, the highlight for me being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:50.940
Sanji’s and Zoro’s teamup in the last episode&nbsp;
and the perfect copy of the Zoro Mihawk fight.

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:57.180
And speaking of visual elements, the special&nbsp;
effects in this show were really spectacular.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:03.300
Buggy’s CGI and that of the sea king were insanely&nbsp;
well done, and just overall, there was a great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:09.420
mix between physical and digital effects being&nbsp;
used. Two notable exceptions to this, that stood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:15.420
out really weirdly were Zoro’s swords shattering&nbsp;
after his clash with Mihawk, only that it looked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:23.280
like really bad CGI and the second time was Chu&nbsp;
catching fire in his fight with Usopp, where it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:29.220
looks like the just set a mannequin on fire and&nbsp;
it suddenly keels over in the wrong direction. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:36.900
fact in contrast to all the fantastic and flawless&nbsp;
effects up to this point, this scene made me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:43.680
actually laugh out loud for how much it stood out.
And another thing, that was consistently great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:48.780
throughout the show were the locations and&nbsp;
islands. Logue Town looked just insane.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:54.540
luffy’s home fusha village looked perfect, same&nbsp;
goes for the Marine base and syrup village. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.540 --> 00:05:00.060
most importantly, the show really managed to bring&nbsp;
these places to live, like the secret safe and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:07.800
map room inside Morgan’s marine base in this first&nbsp;
episode. Really the only exception to this for me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:13.260
was Nami’s hometown Cocoyashi village in the last&nbsp;
2 episodes. Even though all of these locations had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:19.800
a unique and fresh take on them, Nami’s hometown&nbsp;
missed that feeling of small village in paradise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:24.540
that is secretly tormented by Arlong. Whatever&nbsp;
this is [show the village from episode 7 or 8]&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:31.680
that’s just a bit too rural for me. But speaking&nbsp;
of the changes to the island, you probably also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:38.340
noticed, that overall the entire one piece world&nbsp;
has been a little bit modernized in this show. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:44.400
party bar in Luffy’s flashback has neon lights,&nbsp;
electricity DOES seems to be a regular thing in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:51.540
this version of One Piece, and many of the outfits&nbsp;
in the series are just modern day cloths. Now I am&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:58.200
personally a little bit torn about this decision&nbsp;
to be completely honest. On the one hand i do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:05.340
really dig the overall aesthetic, plus there&nbsp;
actually IS a large variety of technological&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:11.640
levels in the One Piece Manga. But at the same&nbsp;
time, part of the original stories charm is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:17.700
most places in the one piece world are stuck&nbsp;
in a pre or at max mid-industrialization era,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:23.760
where only unique places in the Grandline have&nbsp;
access to advanced technology with the exception&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:30.480
of the world government, who uses their technical&nbsp;
knowledge to rule over the world. But again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:36.300
aesthetically it’s a really cool take&nbsp;
on the world and i can roll with it.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:42.540
And speaking of Luffy’s childhood flashback: I&nbsp;
have very divided feelings. And I’ll start with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:49.380
the negative this time: I personally don’t buy&nbsp;
neither Shanks nor his first mate Ben Beckman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:56.520
For Ben Beckman, nothing against the actor, but&nbsp;
this is one of the very few bad castings in my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.520 --> 00:07:03.420
opinion. This guy neither looks nor feels like&nbsp;
the tall, chill and lean guy we know from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:10.080
story. As for Shanks, I think the actor Peter&nbsp;
Gadiot looks quite a lot like Shanks and also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:17.760
did a good job portraying him, but his costume&nbsp;
was just off. The straw hat is just too small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:23.760
and doesn’t look as worn as it should after&nbsp;
being passed down to him by Roger. Of course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:30.240
I absolutely loved Shanks doing a finger gun&nbsp;
towards the mountain bandit and Lucky Roo firing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:36.360
the shot. That was pretty cool. Also the final&nbsp;
scene with him and Mihawk that they perfectly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:42.300
copied from the Manga was really nicely done.&nbsp;
And this has nothing to do with Shanks per se,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:47.760
but the way they showed his conquerors haki&nbsp;
to shoo away the sea king was a little bit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:55.020
underwhelming i found. It could have used&nbsp;
a lot more power and gravity, visually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.020 --> 00:08:01.680
but also sound wise. And next to Shanks and&nbsp;
Ben Beckman, I personally also found that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:09.540
portrayal of Kid Luffy missed the mark by quite&nbsp;
a bit. Instead of being head strong and a bit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:16.080
of a pest, like in the Anime, this version&nbsp;
of Luffy is a lot less cheerful and comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:21.480
across more like a bit of crybaby. Though let&nbsp;
me know if you thought that it worked for you.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:28.080
That being said though, I do personally think,&nbsp;
that the flashbacks were one of the absolute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:35.940
best parts of the entire season. All of them were&nbsp;
kept extremely close to the raw material and all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:42.300
of them had at least the same emotional impact as&nbsp;
in the anime, and I’ll be honest some of them even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:48.060
surpasses the original. Seeing Usopp losing his&nbsp;
mother, while his dad is off partying with Shanks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:54.720
actually made me tear up seeing it happen to&nbsp;
an actual kid. Sanji’s flashback with Zeff was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.720 --> 00:09:00.060
insanely dark and gruesome, especially showing&nbsp;
the remaining blood and flesh on the rock where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:07.920
Zeff had cut off his leg and eaten it. And, oh&nbsp;
my god, don’t even get me started on Nami’s. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:13.200
Belemere looks a little to old here I think&nbsp;
and yes they didn’t straight out show her being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:22.920
shot in the head by Arlong, like in the Manga,&nbsp;
but honestly it was heavy enough as is. All of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:28.200
these flashbacks made me truly care and empathize&nbsp;
with this version of the straw hats once again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:34.380
so it might not be a big surprises for you when&nbsp;
I tell you that the backstories were one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:39.780
most important things in this show to get&nbsp;
100% correct for the author Eiichiro Oda.

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:46.920
And in fact, I think that most characters in the&nbsp;
show have been portrayed almost perfectly. Mihawk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:51.540
Helmeppo, Koby, Zeff, Nami, Sanji, Usopp, and of&nbsp;
course we’ll also get to all the villains in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:57.060
moment as well. Also, I will admit, that halway&nbsp;
thorough the first episode during the bar scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.060 --> 00:10:04.020
I switched from English to the Japanese Dub,&nbsp;
which for me personally made ton of stuff work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:09.540
really really really well throughout the rest of&nbsp;
the show, that seemed to be a bit cringe, at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:16.080
from what i saw from the English subtitles. So&nbsp;
yeah, having the actual voice actors of everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:22.560
made the entire thing incredibly enjoyable to&nbsp;
me and sold me a lot of scenes way more than the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:28.500
English original might have. But coming back to my&nbsp;
list of perfect characters, you might notice that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:35.160
i didn’t list 2 characters in particular here:&nbsp;
Luffy and Zoro. And actually for Luffy it’s really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:41.220
only some minor things that bug me a little.&nbsp;
For one, I just don’t vibe with some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:46.740
humor they wrote for him, though some stuff was&nbsp;
absolutely hilarious, especially his interaction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:55.740
with Buggy. Similarly, some of Luffy’s CGI was a&nbsp;
bit meh, like him dodging Alveida’s club, while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.740 --> 00:11:01.680
other stuff like his head butt against Kuro or of&nbsp;
course his gomu gomu axe that took down arlong and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:08.280
his park were done exceptionally well. My biggest&nbsp;
issues I had with Luffy though were once when he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:14.640
is captured in the water tank by Buggy, where he&nbsp;
looks genuinely scared for his life, which is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:21.660
not very Luffy like and a second time when Zoro is&nbsp;
unconscious after being defeated by Mihawk. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:27.720
I personally don’t mind them showing how&nbsp;
much Luffy cares for his nakama. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:35.160
he really really does. We know that. But the way&nbsp;
Luffy behaves and over reacts here just doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:41.220
seem like something that real Luffy would do.&nbsp;
Other than that though I’m more than happy to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:48.360
say that Iñaki Godoy did a good job bringing a&nbsp;
character to live, that is really really hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:53.520
to actually bring to live and I’m also more than&nbsp;
happy to admit, that often enough he hit the right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.520 --> 00:12:01.200
tone in such a way, that I couldn’t help but grin.
Which now brings me to maybe the biggest criticism&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:08.460
I have of the entire show, which is my favorite&nbsp;
character in the entire series: Roronoa Zoro.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:13.620
First off, to get it out of the way, visually,&nbsp;
the casting and costume of Zoro are flawless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:19.860
No complaints here. But oh boy does it go downhill&nbsp;
from here for me. Because for me this is not Zoro,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:26.400
but what someone cosplaying Zoro would be like.&nbsp;
Now to be clear, I don’t really know if this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:32.580
to blame on the writing staff or on Makenyu’s&nbsp;
acting, or both maybe, but this character just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:40.620
feels like a really big disappointing miss to me.&nbsp;
The Zoro I and many people in the world love and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.620 --> 00:12:47.400
respect so much, is cool, not because he says&nbsp;
cool things and doesn’t cry. It’s because Zoro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:53.880
is someone who belives so strongly in his own&nbsp;
power, but also in his path as a swordsman, that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.880 --> 00:13:01.140
he genuinely doesn’t care what people think about&nbsp;
him. NOW THAT’S COOL. And when he actually cares,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:07.860
it gives his character so much depth. Crying after&nbsp;
being defeated by Mihawk and swearing his loyalty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:17.340
to Luffy the future pirate king, that scene in&nbsp;
the live action was just a shadow of that. Zoro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:24.000
being rescued by Luffy last second and deciding to&nbsp;
dedicate himself to this goofy captain: Scratched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:30.720
completely. Luffy unties him, then leaves again&nbsp;
and then they fight Morgan together. In the manga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:37.440
Zoro willingly lets himself be tied for a month&nbsp;
to protect a little girl. In the live action,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:46.380
he protects the girl and then just lets himself&nbsp;
get tied up for no reason at all? Also, yes Zoro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:53.040
in the Anime is a lot more ruthless than Luffy and&nbsp;
is willing to kill, but this Zoro we get is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.040 --> 00:14:01.620
insane. Cutting people in half and he actually&nbsp;
says that he wants to kill Mihawk. As if killing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:07.620
Mihawk was necessary to Zoro’s dream. Now i’m not&nbsp;
saying Zoro would NEVER kill Mihawk in the manga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:14.220
but clearly his goal is to beat him in a duel of&nbsp;
skill to take his title, not by killing him. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:20.640
yeah the entire, I don’l laugh because I’m to cool&nbsp;
thing, to me feels like someone who is overflowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:26.160
with insecurity, not like the coolest character&nbsp;
in the world, who doesn’t care about anything.

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:34.020
His counterpart Sanji on the other hand:&nbsp;
Chefskiss. No pun intended. The scenes with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:38.160
him on the Baratie and with Zeff are&nbsp;
perfect, and just like in the Manga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:44.760
once he joins the crew his chemistry with&nbsp;
the rest of the straw hats is insane.

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:51.180
Which brings me to the other big thing that&nbsp;
will be controversial about this adaption:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.380 --> 00:15:00.660
They did end up changing A LOT, and I mean A LOT&nbsp;
more than I ever anticipated. We get more Buggy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:07.680
who was without any doubt the standout performance&nbsp;
of this season. Incredibly well done, first making&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:14.520
him terrifying and then giving him the comedic&nbsp;
twist, we all wanted. But then there is a bunch of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:20.940
stuff that I thought was not necessary to change&nbsp;
and that took away a bit from my experience:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:28.800
First, we had not 1, but 2 entire episodes of a&nbsp;
freddy Kruger style teenage horror thing inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:36.540
the mansion on Syrup village. Kuro was portrayed&nbsp;
fantastically, but I think this entire arc could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:44.460
have been done with in 30 minutes, not&nbsp;
120. Instead of Usopp saving his village,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:52.860
he does …nothing? in his own arc. instead Nami&nbsp;
and Kaya got the emotional part. And even though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:59.160
Zoro got a great flashback as everyone else,&nbsp;
it was really weirdly placed in a 30 minute&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:06.060
strangely overly dramatic battle trying to climb&nbsp;
out of a well. You know, instead of saving it for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:12.120
his clash with Mihawk, but whatever. Also&nbsp;
I feel like the show really missed out on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:21.000
building some real suspense and mystery for the&nbsp;
audience. It’s obvious Kuro is the bad guy like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:26.220
5 minutes into the episode. Similarly later&nbsp;
on Nami betraying the straw hats and revealing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:32.460
herself as part of Arlongs crew could be such&nbsp;
a big shock moment for new fans. Instead it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:38.520
made painfully obvious multiple times, that she&nbsp;
doesn’t want to go, before she actually leaves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.520 --> 00:16:44.580
while also saving Luffy’s life and blaming&nbsp;
him for Zoro almost dying. Anyways… The next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:49.260
big change was of course to have Arlong and&nbsp;
the fishmen appear way earlier in the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:55.200
which honestly I think worked really well, had it&nbsp;
not been for that weird weird fight between Arlong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:55.200 --> 00:17:01.860
and Luffy at the Baratie where he completely&nbsp;
wiped the floor with Luffy. And of course the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:01.860 --> 00:17:07.680
biggest change of all: Garp being the main Marine&nbsp;
antagonist, chasing Luffy throught the east blue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:13.380
And while I actually really like the idea of this&nbsp;
as a concept, basically taking Garps interaction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:20.760
with the straw hats on Water 7 and weaving it into&nbsp;
the early story here, the execution was not that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:26.040
well done I think. First we are meant to believe&nbsp;
that Garp seriously wants to capture Luffy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:33.300
but cant. which we know given how powerful Garp&nbsp;
is would be no problem whatsoever for him. Then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:33.300 --> 00:17:40.200
at the end it’s supposed to have all been a test&nbsp;
to see if Luffy was ready? So you sent Mihawk to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:46.260
capture Luffy, as a test? What? Also, neither of&nbsp;
these make sense for Garps character. He’s not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.260 --> 00:17:54.900
the type to actually try and capture his grandson,&nbsp;
but he also isn’t the type to make sure luffy is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:59.880
ready to become the next pirate king. Otherwise he&nbsp;
actually would have been there in the manga. Still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:06.600
I did enjoy the chemistry between the characters&nbsp;
and seeing Garp interact with Mihawk and Zeff.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:10.500
With that being said though, even though yes,&nbsp;
there was a bunch of things to complain about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:15.720
with the One Piece live action, in the great&nbsp;
scheme of things as someone who was extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:22.740
skeptical of this project, my expectations have&nbsp;
been blown away. Even if not perfect and against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:28.860
my biggest fears, this show was really fun to&nbsp;
watch, got me involved with its characters and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:34.380
most importantly really felt like watching One&nbsp;
Piece come to live in a way. It made me cry, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:39.840
made me laugh and most importantly, I finished the&nbsp;
last scene with a big grin on my face. Here is my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:46.740
list of ratings for each episode, overall bringing&nbsp;
the show to a really solid 7.5 / 10 score for me.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:54.420
I’m really happy my favorite series now has a new&nbsp;
interpretation and i very much hope there will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.420 --> 00:19:03.480
a season 2. In the meantime, here is another&nbsp;
video for you to watch. Shanks for watching.

